# shortest_routes_single_source:
# CSES 1671, Shortest Routes I (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1671), in our
# own words: city_count cities and one-way flights, each from a city to another with a
# positive cost; the least total cost of a trip from city 1 to each city, the
# answer the sum of these city_count costs (CSES asks the list of the costs; the
# sum keeps the work and makes the answer one number, where the list of 10^5
# costs at the top rung made a point's answer and its traps tens of megabytes).
# CSES promises that every city can be reached; for a city that cannot, this
# program counts the total cost of all flights plus one, which no trip costs.
# Part of the CSES port's second batch.
#
# INPUT: the number of cities, a binary natural (corpora/library/binary/natural),
# and the flights, a Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of triples
# `pair from (pair to cost)` (corpora/library/prelude/pair), each a positive
# binary natural. The answer is a binary natural.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: a trip of total cost exactly trip_cost
# reaches the city (reaches trip_cost city) when trip_cost = 0 and the city is city 1, or when some flight
# from a city intermediate to the city of cost <= trip_cost has a trip of cost trip_cost - cost to intermediate, by its
# recursion on trip_cost (every cost is positive, so trip_cost - cost < trip_cost); the least cost of a
# trip to the city is the least trip_cost, counted up from 0 while trip_cost stays within the total
# cost total of all flights (a shortest trip uses no flight twice), for which
# reaches trip_cost city holds, and total + 1 when none does. Under tabling the reading shares
# reaches trip_cost city for each trip_cost and city, about city_count total flight_count steps for flight_count flights; the
# replacement the family asks for is Dijkstra's algorithm with a priority
# queue, about (city_count + flight_count) log city_count steps, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only, with no top, no choice and no parallel. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the sum of the costs (reaches consumes trip_cost, the
# search consumes total - trip_cost, the sum consumes city_count - city, each fold
# a finite list, and every flight costs at least 1, as the problem states, so the
# argument trip_cost - cost of the recursive call is smaller than trip_cost).
# binary_subtract, which writes no top
# (../common/binary_modular), is never asked for less than zero, since the
# program subtracts only a cost that is no larger. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by
# the soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of
# Definition 14 (Lean `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`):
# V is an answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then
# V ⊑_O W, while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and
# W to λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and
# the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ binary_subtract _ _
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_odd binary_zero))
λ one
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ flights
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self sum rest
        . rest sum λ flight others. flight λ origin destination_and_cost. destination_and_cost λ destination cost. self (merge_binary_plus sum cost) others
      ) binary_zero flights
  )
λ total_cost
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ flights
    . fixpoint
    λ self trip_cost city
    . ( λ any
        . trip_cost (merge_binary_equality city one) (λ_. any flights) λ_. any flights
      )
    λ
    . fixpoint
    λ any rest
    . rest false
    λ flight others
    . flight
    λ origin destination_and_cost
    . destination_and_cost
    λ destination cost
    . merge_binary_equality destination city (binary_less_than trip_cost cost (any others) (self (binary_subtract trip_cost cost false) origin true (any others))) (any others)
  )
λ reaches
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ flights total city
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self trip_cost
        . binary_less_than total trip_cost trip_cost (reaches flights trip_cost city trip_cost (self (merge_binary_increment trip_cost)))
      ) binary_zero
  )
λ distance
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ city_count flights
    . ( λ total
        . fixpoint
          ( λ self city
            . binary_less_than city_count city binary_zero (merge_binary_plus (distance flights total city) (self (merge_binary_increment city)))
          ) one
      ) (total_cost flights)
  )
λ shortest_routes_single_source
. export shortest_routes_single_source
